# Copy to .env.local (or set in the deployment environment) and fill in real values.
# `.env*.local` is gitignored; never commit real credentials.

# --- Application runtime (.env.local, managed by `vercel env pull`) ---

# Postgres on a standalone Neon project (not the Vercel Marketplace integration —
# see docs/decisions/0007-standalone-neon-instead-of-vercel-managed.md).
# Use the POOLED connection string (hostname contains "-pooler"), and the least-privilege
# `app_designs` role — NOT the database owner. That role holds SELECT/INSERT/UPDATE on `designs`
# and nothing else, so it cannot drop, truncate or delete. See
# docs/decisions/0008-least-privilege-database-role.md.
DATABASE_URL=

# Vercel Blob store holding the scheduled design-table exports (private access).
BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=

# Shared secret Vercel Cron sends as `Authorization: Bearer <value>` to the backup endpoint.
CRON_SECRET=

# Opt-in for the internal capture route `/internal/scene-shot`, which is verification tooling and
# not a customer surface. Unset (or any other value) means a production build serves 404 there;
# set it to exactly `1` only in an environment where the fidelity capture harness must run.
# `apps/web/scripts/capture-fidelity.mjs` sets it on the server it spawns, so local capture needs
# nothing here. Leave it UNSET in the deployed application.
# LEMNARIA_ENABLE_SCENE_SHOT_ROUTE=

# --- Migrations only (.env.migration.local, NOT .env.local) ---
# The owner-role connection. Migrations need DDL rights that DATABASE_URL's role deliberately
# lacks, which is why this is a separate variable rather than a fallback: the running application
# must never hold credentials that can drop a table. Used by `pnpm --filter
# @lemnaria/persistence run migrate`.
# MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL=

# --- Tests only (.env.test.local, NOT .env.local) ---
# A database live tests may write to and delete from. Must not be the application database:
# resolveTestDatabaseUrl() refuses to run if it resolves to the same database as DATABASE_URL.
# See docs/decisions/0006-tests-never-touch-the-application-database.md.
# TEST_DATABASE_URL=
